WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:03.167
We will use one question for the entire build.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:07.382
Order one zero four two was delivered twenty days ago.

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:09.327
Can I still return it?

00:00:09.327 --> 00:00:13.117
The policy source contains the general return rule.

00:00:13.117 --> 00:00:17.023
The order source contains the authoritative delivery information.

00:00:17.473 --> 00:00:19.860
That gives each function a clear job.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.250
The retriever finds the policy.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.380
The order tool returns structured facts.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.470
The grader checks whether evidence is sufficient.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.321
The generator combines approved evidence into a final answer.

00:00:33.135 --> 00:00:37.717
Using one scenario throughout a tutorial reduces cognitive load.

00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:43.949
You can see how the architecture changes without also learning a new problem on every slide.
